I commented on and closed the two issues this session's commits fixed, and left the other ten alone because I did no work on them.

• #1197 (closed, fixed in ac36402b): config show and config get mask github_token2, slack_tokens and tokenvalue again.
  • The rule: a key is masked if its name contains a credential word anywhere, unless it is on an exact-match list of known keys. That list has one entry, max_tokens.
  • The check you suggested: I compared old and new rules over 1080 generated names. None of the 696 names an earlier rule masked print their value now. A deliberately broken version of the rule made the test fail, so the test does catch a leak.
  • Also fixed: names with no credential word in them, like auth_bearer, openai_pat and session_cookie, are masked too.
• #1173 (closed, fixed in 70eefa85): Bedrock Claude runs now send an explicit maxTokens taken from yoagent's model preset (64000 for anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6). That is above the thinking budget of 8192.
  • What's proven: the test server that records the request shows the field going out. It was missing before.
  • What isn't: that Bedrock accepts the new request and would have rejected the old one comes from AWS's and Anthropic's docs. Nothing was sent to real AWS.
  • Left to yoagent upstream (#1198): a user --max-tokens at or below the thinking budget is still sent unchanged, and the /side and architect agents still send no maxTokens on Bedrock.

